      "side": 1,
      "message": "Following the loop bound here: it runs to PKVM_NR_MOVEABLE_REGS rather than pkvm_moveable_regs_nr, and the unused entries are zeroed, so get_region(0) matches the first free slot and returns it instead of NULL.\n\ndev_addr comes straight from a host register in handle___pkvm_init_its_emulation, and that hcall stays callable after deprivilege, so the !its_reg guard in pkvm_init_gic_its_emulation does not hold. With dev_addr 0 we donate the two host pages, set base to __hyp_va(0), and then readq_relaxed(base + GITS_CREADR) is an EL2 access on an address that is not a GIC region at all.\n\nCould the loop be bounded by pkvm_moveable_regs_nr, and the region\u0027s type checked before it is used?",
      "revId": "c7a78521b326ad9181dfa6137daae9734f62898c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
